{
  "_meta": {
    "story": "2.0-D3 T1 — bounded Application Insights read scope",
    "purpose": "Deterministic offline fixtures for the D3 read scope. The POSITIVE set is the four operational signal kinds D3 ingests; the NEGATIVE set is the raw telemetry and analytics output D3 must never ingest (AC2 is proved by seeding these, not by asserting a docstring).",
    "surfaces": "Every positive record is shaped as it arrives on a surface MSP-B2 ALREADY reads: Microsoft.AlertsManagement/alerts (alerts) or Microsoft.ResourceHealth/events (health). D3 adds no surface.",
    "status": "STRUCTURAL SCAFFOLD — shapes follow the Azure common alert schema and the ResourceHealth event shape, and are sufficient to pin classification and scope defence. They are not evidence that a live Application Insights tenant emits these exact field values.",
    "component": "The monitored application is the Application Insights component /subscriptions/11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555/resourceGroups/prod/providers/microsoft.insights/components/prod-checkout-api"
  },

